# Driver — environment variables
# Copy to `.env` and fill in your own values. `.env` is gitignored.

# Backend API base URL. No trailing slash and no version suffix — the app
# appends `/api/v2/drivers/...` itself. The socket connects to the same origin.
#
# There is no mock mode any more. Sign-in is a real phone number and a real
# six-digit code from `POST /api/v2/drivers/auth/start` — and that code is a
# REAL SMS in development too. `infrastructure/sms/sms.js` calls the live
# gateway whatever NODE_ENV says, so sign in with a number you own: an invented
# ten-digit Indian mobile number belongs to somebody, and they get the text.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5001

# Which build this is: development | preview | production.
#
# Decides whether the app narrates itself to the console (`services/log.ts`)
# — off in production, since a failed fetch, socket drop or location fix is
# logged with the error it came from, and that error can carry a rider's own
# job, address and earnings details.
#
# LEAVE IT EMPTY under Metro: it is inferred as development from `__DEV__`.
# A release build must set it to `production` explicitly — an unset value in
# a shipped build is also treated as production, so a forgotten variable
# fails safe rather than leaving logging on.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=

# Google Maps, for the active-job map (`components/ui/MapPanel.tsx`).
#
# Baked into the native binary by `app.config.js`, not read at JS runtime — a
# fresh `eas build` / `expo prebuild` is needed after this changes, and a
# reload alone will not pick it up. Unset leaves the native map view with no
# imagery to draw; the distance readout and everything else on the screen
# still works.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# "Fill with dummy data" on the sign-up steps.
#
# On by default in development (`__DEV__`), off in a shipped build. Set this to
# `true` to keep it in a preview or internal build — for a demo, or for QA on a
# device where `__DEV__` is false. Leave it unset for anything a real partner
# will install: a rider who found the button would file an application an
# approver then has to reject.
#
# It never invents the three fields an account is identified by — the mobile
# number, the email address and the date of birth. See constants/dummyPartner.ts.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ALLOW_DUMMY_DATA=
